  annotation "note_1771589311145_0", anchor: "Twelve footprints frozen in the ice below", text: "I am constitutionally suspicious of round numbers. But ritual arrays at comparable Communion sites preserve exactly these counts in the deep ice — fixed-interval patterns, twelve positions. Sometimes a number is not rhetoric. Sometimes it is simply all the feet that were there.", type: :skepticism, display: :popout
  annotation "note_1771589311145_1", anchor: "The thing beneath the ice pressed upward like attention, like patient hunger, like a kind of recognition the Apex had never wanted", text: "Patient. Watchful. I have catalogued these words, in this arrangement, from deep-ice impressions predating penguin civilization. The Communion did not summon what presses here. They removed what stood between it and us. The Nightshelf claim the watchers are real. This text, without knowing the term, agrees.", type: :commentary, display: :full
  annotation "note_1771589311145_2", anchor: "the pause between cleansing and return", text: "What the Long Dark does seasonally to the boundary between the living world and the ice-memory, desecrated ground does permanently. This 'pause' is not metaphor. It is a condition — the veil cut rather than thinned, held open by what was done here. The Apex exists inside it still.", type: :commentary, display: :popout
  annotation "note_1771589311145_3", anchor: "could read ice the way other penguins read faces, could tell where a fissure would run before the first pick struck", text: "I know this work. Reading ice with the body — with breath and flipper-pressure and the knowledge of where crystal wants to break. To lose it is not to lose a skill. It is to lose a language you spoke before you had words. The ice still talks. You stand there and it says nothing back.", type: :tangent, display: :full
